Testing SSH Connection
Ensure that you have the SSH client installed on your system (such as OpenSSH).
Open a terminal or command prompt.
Run the SSH connection command: ssh -T git@github.com
Replace git@github.com with the appropriate SSH URL for the server you want to connect to.
If this is your first time connecting to the server, you may see a message asking you to confirm the server's authenticity. Type "yes" to proceed.
If you have set up SSH keys correctly and they are properly configured on the server, you will see a success message or a welcome message from the server.
If the connection is not successful, ensure that your SSH keys are set up correctly and that you have provided the correct SSH URL for the server.
